  "instance_name": "shrimp_flavor_popsicle_stereotype",
  "label": "Shrimp-flavored popsicle stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the absurdity of comparing a sweet, sugary treat (popsicle) to the taste of shrimp, which is typically considered savory, briny, and seafood-based. This juxtaposition is inherently humorous because it violates common expectations of flavor pairing, creating a shock value that is central to the meme's comedic effect. The stereotype here is not of a specific group but of the general human experience of taste perception and the expectation of sweetness in ice cream or popsicles.",
